+# Pickup reminders
+
+For whoever changes how members are reminded, or is about to propose email reminders to save the SMS cost. The day
+before a pickup, larder texts the member their pickup slot. Reminders go by SMS, about 40 euros a month, because
+email was tried and members missed more pickups: written after issue 52, the third proposal to switch in 2025.
+
+## Message
+
+`larder/reminders.py` sends one message the day before the pickup: "Your pantry order is ready for pickup
+<slot>." to the member's phone.
+
+## Channel
+
+The channel is `CHANNEL` in `larder/reminders.py`; it is `"sms"`, and any other value sends the same message by
+email instead.
+
+Reminders went by email from April to June 2025 to save the SMS cost. The email provider's report showed 34% of the
+reminder emails never opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% of pantry orders to 13%. Each missed pickup is a
+packed bag whose fresh food is thrown away at closing time. Many members share one phone across the family and never
+check email; a text they see. Reminders went back to SMS on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups were back to 6% by
+August.
+
+A proposal to move reminders off SMS has to answer those numbers: the saving is 40 euros a month, and the email
+trial doubled the missed pickups.
